# tally 2.2.1 (#212, S-212), L §5.16: a decision reads a random fact "through a projection only for an amount booked on
# or before that day"; L §5.14.1: "A random amount dated after t is read as §5.16 says". save[m], on the month's
# second day, projects konto at mean; spend[m] is dated the month's second-last day, its law date the month's first:
# the projection reads its amount at its distribution's mean, never the path's sample, so konto isn't held at keep on
# every path (m_konto, one). tally 2.2 took the sample by the fact's law date: m_konto 100 PLN with standard error 0
# (the simplification review's r1b.tally).
=== r1b.tally
model r1
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-04-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input shock[m in months]: dist PLN
input keep: money PLN
input pay: money PLN

move wage[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

move spend[m in months]: transfers
  on end_of(m) - 1 day
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount round(shock[m], minor(PLN), half-even)

move save[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m) + 1 day
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to sav amount max(0 PLN, round(min(bal(konto, d) from (start_of(m) + 1 day) random at mean for d in start_of(m) + 1 day .. end_of(m) - 1 day step 1 day), minor(PLN), half-even) - keep)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  keep = 100.00 PLN "s"
  pay = 1000.00 PLN "s"
  shock[*] = uniform(200 PLN, 600 PLN) to 0.01 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask m_sav: mean(bal(sav, 2026-03-31)) paths 8 seed 3
ask m_konto: mean(bal(konto, 2026-03-31)) paths 8 seed 3
ask one: bal(sav, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) paths 8 seed 3 path 2
ask proj_mean: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-01 random at mean
ask proj_q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-01 random at quantile(0.9)
=== expect m_sav m_konto one
m_sav: 1 736.8875 PLN (standard error 74.098727; 8 paths; horizon none)
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-01-02
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-02-02
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-03-02
  cut 2026-01-01
m_konto: 152.295 PLN (standard error 41.117534; 8 paths; horizon none)
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-01-02
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-02-02
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-03-02
  cut 2026-01-01
one: (1 485.78 PLN, 191.25 PLN)
  sample: shock[2026-01] = 551.48 PLN (u = 0.87870451890858247221273262528296044138187426142394542694091796875 (0.878704518908582))
  sample: shock[2026-02] = 462.74 PLN (u = 0.65684362106157429962824574609658867530015413649380207061767578125 (0.656843621061574))
  sample: shock[2026-03] = 308.75 PLN (u = 0.27187652637924711028515924182702434563907445408403873443603515625 (0.271876526379247))
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-01-02
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-02-02
  left out: save, 1 instances, first 2026-03-02
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-NEGATIVE konto is below zero from 2026-01-31
warning: WARN-NEGATIVE konto is below zero from 2026-02-28
warning: WARN-NEGATIVE konto is below zero from 2026-03-31
warning: WARN-NEGATIVE konto is below zero from 2026-04-30
